WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.740
Consider a rack that fits its supports and has adequate electrical capacity,

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.560
but cannot sustain the requested workload because the receiving loop doesn't meet

3
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.900
the required thermal conditions.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.760
The mechanical and power checks can remain valid while the operating case

5
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.280
fails.

6
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.740
Trace the heat path to locate the actual boundary mismatch.

7
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.420
Don't immediately blame the coupling or install a larger power shelf.

8
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.060
A change to flow, temperature, heat rejection or the equipment envelope must

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.660
be supported by the responsible design and site teams.

10
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.220
The review decision is to hold the unsupported operating case.

11
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.060
A reduced or bounded activity may be possible only with its own

12
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.840
justified conditions and restrictions.

13
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.660
Record what evidence would close the thermal gap.

14
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.360
The linked Project Brazos material offers relevant context for cooling integration in

15
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.600
an existing facility, but it doesn't replace this site's commitments.

16
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.460
A rack is a system of interfaces precisely because a pass in

17
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.420
one domain cannot compensate for a blocking gap in another.

